    "question": {
      ":question/id": "437b7012-074f-5fc1-a4f6-32cc935a9a27",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The matrices $A$ and $B$ are upper triangular matrices since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $C$ and $D$ and $E$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =-2\\ne 0 \\\\ {d}_{21} & =3\\ne 0 \\\\ {e}_{21} & =4\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
